WEBVTT

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:11.801
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.881 --> 00:00:17.601
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:21.291
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:29.021
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:33.361
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:35.241
But, with you...

00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:37.321
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.161 --> 00:00:42.911
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.081 --> 00:00:47.631
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:52.011
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.011 --> 00:00:53.591
Just to survive!

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:55.551
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:57.391
Take this moment...

00:00:57.391 --> 00:01:01.011
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:03.221
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:05.061
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:08.771
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:10.901
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.611
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.611 --> 00:01:16.281
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.281 --> 00:01:18.451
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.451 --> 00:01:20.281
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.281 --> 00:01:24.201
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:47.908
Good morning!

00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:51.445
I've been accepted!

00:01:52.013 --> 00:01:53.347
C-congratulations…

00:01:53.814 --> 00:01:56.417
Alright! I'm the first to arrive at DDS!

00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:00.888
Hey, wait! You'll need this! Hey!

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.230
Wow! They have some huge trees here.

00:02:19.607 --> 00:02:21.008
Awesome!

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.779
Woohoo! I'm so excited!

00:02:25.713 --> 00:02:27.048
Hey! Kyuu!

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:29.683
Good morning!

00:02:31.118 --> 00:02:31.786
Good morning!

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:36.157
You're early. The matriculation ceremony
doesn't start for a while.

00:02:36.223 --> 00:02:41.328
Heh, you may say that, but didn't you come
in early to explore the campus as well?

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:42.930
Well, yeah…

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.799
I guess we were all thinking the same thing.

00:02:45.232 --> 00:02:47.501
Well, let's get to it!

00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:56.210
Huh?

00:02:56.277 --> 00:02:59.580
What's en simulation classroom?

00:03:00.281 --> 00:03:01.549
Let's take a look inside.

00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:18.232
This is like the set of & monster movie.

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:19.867
Wow!

00:03:20.568 --> 00:03:25.206
These miniatures are probably used
to reproduce crime scenes.

00:03:27.842 --> 00:03:29.510
What does this switch do?

00:03:34.615 --> 00:03:37.451
Looks like you can control the weather in this room.

00:03:41.322 --> 00:03:44.258
Kyuu! How dare you!

00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:45.926
S-sorry...

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:51.499
Looks like this is a martial arts practice hall.

00:03:51.532 --> 00:03:54.935
When it comes to the crunch, detectives
have to use their fists.

00:03:56.337 --> 00:03:57.571
What about this room?

00:03:57.938 --> 00:04:00.407
This is probably a forensics lab.

00:04:06.113 --> 00:04:09.049
A-A corpse!

00:04:10.618 --> 00:04:12.286
It's just a doll.

00:04:12.553 --> 00:04:15.723
This simulation is for us to practice determining
the presumed time of death.

00:04:16.657 --> 00:04:17.458
And this is?

00:04:17.892 --> 00:04:20.327
The sign said "Special Disguise Room".

00:04:21.996 --> 00:04:23.564
What's this for then?

00:04:23.731 --> 00:04:24.765
This is awesome!

00:04:25.332 --> 00:04:26.800
There are lots of different classrooms!

00:04:28.536 --> 00:04:31.772
Hey, it's almost time for them to
announce the class divisions.

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:33.240
Class divisions?

00:04:33.474 --> 00:04:35.009
Didn't you know?

00:04:35.576 --> 00:04:40.648
At DDS, incoming students are divided into classes
A to D according to their entrance exam scores.

00:04:41.081 --> 00:04:43.017
Really? Is that right?

00:04:44.752 --> 00:04:48.589
Every year the class divisions
are posted on this billboard.

00:04:57.631 --> 00:04:58.365
Good morning!

00:04:58.599 --> 00:04:59.733
So you guys really came.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.303
Oh! Katagiri-san, er I mean, Sensei.

00:05:03.037 --> 00:05:04.371
Good morning!

00:05:08.075 --> 00:05:10.578
Mister! That was you back then…

00:05:11.078 --> 00:05:11.979
The mountain climber!

00:05:21.655 --> 00:05:22.890
We meet again.

00:05:27.595 --> 00:05:32.800
This is Dan Morihiko-sensei, the founder
and current headmaster of this school.

00:05:34.235 --> 00:05:37.371
You're that… Legendary detective…

00:05:37.972 --> 00:05:39.340
Dan Morihiko…

00:05:40.007 --> 00:05:42.810
So this is Dan-sensei, the eminent
detective who made it possible…

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:47.014
... for this to be the only school in Japan where you're allowed to bear arms.

00:05:52.186 --> 00:05:54.989
P-please give me your autograph!

00:05:56.457 --> 00:05:58.692
What the heck is Kinta thinking?

00:06:02.296 --> 00:06:04.331
I have great expectations for you guys.

00:06:05.132 --> 00:06:06.300
Good luck.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:07.468
Yes!

00:06:07.768 --> 00:06:08.569
Yes!

00:06:09.637 --> 00:06:11.105
Ah, they're posting the announcements!

00:06:11.739 --> 00:06:12.673
Announcements?

00:06:13.173 --> 00:06:14.675
These are the new Class A students.

00:06:22.416 --> 00:06:25.352
Huh? Our names aren't there.

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:30.924
Ah, I guess we didn't quality for Class A.

00:06:32.092 --> 00:06:32.926
It's Class B!

00:06:35.396 --> 00:06:36.163
That's me!

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:40.868
Not even on the Class B list.

00:06:44.271 --> 00:06:46.840
We're not in Class C either, so…

00:06:48.309 --> 00:06:50.544
Let's have fun in Class D, guys.

00:06:51.345 --> 00:06:55.015
You guys I can understand, but I
can't believe my name wasn't…

00:06:58.352 --> 00:06:59.053
You're kidding me…

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.588
Our names aren't there either.

00:07:02.022 --> 00:07:03.357
That's impossible!

00:07:03.824 --> 00:07:06.593
Are these the right lists?

00:07:06.927 --> 00:07:10.130
Oh my! Can't find your names?

00:07:10.497 --> 00:07:14.068
Perhaps it was just in your dreams
that you guys got accepted.

00:07:15.836 --> 00:07:17.037
Saburoumaru-san!

00:07:17.204 --> 00:07:22.609
Hey now! Starting today, call
me Saburoumaru of Class A.

00:07:38.092 --> 00:07:38.926
Here they are!

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:40.794
But…

00:07:41.261 --> 00:07:41.862
What's wrong?

00:07:42.329 --> 00:07:43.797
What's Class Q?

00:07:49.069 --> 00:07:52.473
It's quite a way from ABCD to Q.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.109
Just a class of substitutes, isn't it?

00:07:56.009 --> 00:07:58.712
What's wrong with that? We still got accepted!

00:07:59.374 --> 00:08:03.474
But, it's still Class Q. Bye now.

00:08:00.549 --> 00:08:03.174
Huh? What's this sheet of paper?

00:08:06.353 --> 00:08:07.388
D-Dan-sensei!

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.191
Look at this!

00:08:12.826 --> 00:08:14.995
To headmaster Dan Morihiko…

00:08:15.796 --> 00:08:17.831
I've planted bombs on your campus.

00:08:17.965 --> 00:08:19.800
This is a challenge to you.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.169
I will provide you with some hints.

00:08:22.403 --> 00:08:24.772
There are three bombs in total.

00:08:25.539 --> 00:08:26.573
The first one will…

00:08:26.874 --> 00:08:29.009
…explode at 8:00 am.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.746
This is… a bomb threat?

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.516
Planted somewhere on the campus?

00:08:36.216 --> 00:08:38.218
Maybe it's some kind of prank.

00:08:39.052 --> 00:08:42.189
Could this also be part of the entrance exam?

00:08:51.465 --> 00:08:52.599
It's already 8:00!

00:09:17.724 --> 00:09:19.159
They've come…

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.234
Dan-sensei…

00:09:27.835 --> 00:09:30.270
Unfortunately, this is not part of the exam.

00:09:32.039 --> 00:09:33.774
Evacuate the students immediately!

00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:34.641
Yes, sir!

00:09:35.275 --> 00:09:37.744
Now, you guys, hurry and get out of here as well.

00:09:38.178 --> 00:09:42.683
Y-You're right. This doesn't seem like a joke.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:48.088
He's right. Bombs being planted at DDS is no joke!

00:09:49.957 --> 00:09:52.893
Dan-sensei. Please let me help too!

00:09:54.094 --> 00:09:57.331
Kyuu-kun, I appreciate your concern, but…

00:09:57.598 --> 00:09:58.932
…you should evacuate for the time being.

00:09:59.867 --> 00:10:00.567
But!

00:10:02.269 --> 00:10:05.038
Dan-sensei! We've caught a suspect!

00:10:17.618 --> 00:10:19.419
Just as expected of DDS.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.422
They've caught the culprit this quickly?

00:10:23.257 --> 00:10:25.659
But, there are still two bomb: left.

00:10:26.026 --> 00:10:27.628
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:10:28.595 --> 00:10:30.430
Where are the remaining bombs?

00:10:32.099 --> 00:10:33.734
Find them yourself.

00:10:34.902 --> 00:10:38.105
Aren't you supposed to be the
best detective in Japan?

00:10:41.008 --> 00:10:45.946
I challenge you to find the other
bombs that I planted.

00:10:47.848 --> 00:10:52.753
My talents are superior to the rest! This is your
punishment for rejecting my superiority!

00:10:53.554 --> 00:10:54.588
Take him away.

00:10:58.158 --> 00:10:58.692
Sensei!

00:11:23.317 --> 00:11:27.020
At this rate, there won't be anybody
left who can find my bomb!

00:11:27.754 --> 00:11:30.390
I'm more talented than anybody else!

00:11:31.191 --> 00:11:34.227
In spite of that, you rejected me. Why?

00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:41.702
The answer to your question will be revealed
when the third bomb fails to explode.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:48.475
We'll see! The third bomb will explode
ten minutes from now!

00:11:49.843 --> 00:11:50.611
Ten minutes!

00:11:51.478 --> 00:11:53.280
The third one is another time bomb?

00:11:54.047 --> 00:11:54.948
Take him away.

00:11:54.948 --> 00:11:55.415
Yes, sir.

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:00.687
Evacuate the students at once!

00:12:01.355 --> 00:12:03.657
That's an order, Katagiri-kun.

00:12:03.757 --> 00:12:04.257
Yes.

00:12:09.296 --> 00:12:15.535
It's just so wrong. The classrooms we explored
this morning might be destroyed.

00:12:25.679 --> 00:12:34.121
We all worked so hard to get here and, now that
we're here, we can't do anything to help.

00:12:36.356 --> 00:12:38.158
Don't give up, Megu.

00:12:38.625 --> 00:12:40.394
That's right! There's still time!

00:12:41.028 --> 00:12:43.096
Let's find the bomb!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:44.264
Kyuu…

00:12:45.766 --> 00:12:48.268
Um… Me too?

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:54.808
O-of course I'll help! This is the DDS I
worked so hard to get into after all!

00:12:57.177 --> 00:13:00.847
There has to be some hint that
will help us find the bomb.

00:13:10.625 --> 00:13:15.530
Why did the culprit stick around
after planting the bombs?

00:13:16.297 --> 00:13:19.167
Staying here would make his chances
of getting caught much higher.

00:13:19.701 --> 00:13:23.371
Even though he said he was so
superior, he's pretty stupid.

00:13:25.239 --> 00:13:28.843
Perhaps the culprit allowed himself
to be caught intentionally.

00:13:29.477 --> 00:13:30.778
But why?

00:13:31.813 --> 00:13:36.017
For example, perhaps he did
that to target Dan-sensei.

00:13:36.784 --> 00:13:37.986
Dan-sensei?

00:13:38.453 --> 00:13:43.091
Come to think of it, that warning letter
was addressed to Dan-sensei.

00:13:44.993 --> 00:13:50.398
The culprit probably intended to lure Dan-sensei out.

00:13:51.065 --> 00:13:53.868
But what it Dan-sensei didn't come?

00:13:55.503 --> 00:13:57.939
That's why he detonated the first bomb!

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:03.411
Surely, with all the commotion and the
way that the threat was addressed…

00:14:03.411 --> 00:14:05.513
…it was very likely that Dan-sensei would come.

00:14:05.947 --> 00:14:08.349
And then, the second bomb exploded…

00:14:11.819 --> 00:14:16.624
Why did the culprit let the bomb
explode right next to himself?

00:14:17.291 --> 00:14:19.193
That's right…

00:14:20.061 --> 00:14:22.597
He could have been hurt too.

00:14:23.131 --> 00:14:25.166
It was quite a powerful bomb too.…

00:14:25.633 --> 00:14:29.404
My hat got blown off somewhere
thanks to that blast!

00:14:30.071 --> 00:14:32.240
No. No. Look on your back!

00:14:33.608 --> 00:14:37.445
See? Your hat. It got hooked on your backpack.

00:14:37.879 --> 00:14:40.448
What the? It was here the whole time!

00:14:44.952 --> 00:14:45.953
That's right…

00:14:46.754 --> 00:14:47.588
I've got it!

00:14:48.956 --> 00:14:50.458
What? You've got it?

00:14:50.958 --> 00:14:52.927
In any case, Dan-sensei is in trouble!

00:14:54.295 --> 00:14:55.196
H-hey!

00:14:55.196 --> 00:14:55.730
Wait up!

00:15:11.112 --> 00:15:13.147
What do you mean, Kyuu?

00:15:13.281 --> 00:15:14.348
There are two hints!

00:15:14.749 --> 00:15:19.520
The first one is the fact that the culprit detonated
the bomb right next to himself.

00:15:20.388 --> 00:15:21.389
And the other hint is.…

00:15:22.323 --> 00:15:24.158
...Kazuma-kun, your hat!

00:15:24.659 --> 00:15:27.361
Huh? My hat?

00:15:27.829 --> 00:15:28.396
Right!

00:15:29.464 --> 00:15:30.598
I still don't get it!

00:15:31.099 --> 00:15:33.301
Oh no! We only have five minutes!

00:15:34.035 --> 00:15:34.969
Dan-sensei!

00:15:35.703 --> 00:15:36.971
Dan-sensei!

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.141
Dan-sensei!

00:15:40.675 --> 00:15:43.244
You guys haven't evacuated yet?

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.416
Excuse me for a second, Dan-sensei!

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.218
Kyuu-kun!

00:15:59.594 --> 00:16:03.097
Sensei, are you carrying something
different than usual?

00:16:03.731 --> 00:16:05.466
Hey, hold on! What do you mean?

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.435
There's only one answer!

00:16:08.102 --> 00:16:10.905
The bomb was planted on Dan-sensei!

00:16:11.239 --> 00:16:13.574
Eh? On Dan-sensei?

00:16:13.741 --> 00:16:14.842
It was planted there?

00:16:16.577 --> 00:16:17.578
Kyuu-kun!

00:16:18.713 --> 00:16:24.652
We assumed that the three bombs had been
planted in advance by the culprit.

00:16:25.153 --> 00:16:33.661
But actually, the third bomb was planted on
Dan-sensei right when the second bomb exploded.

00:16:40.802 --> 00:16:46.007
I see. The culprit planted the
bomb during the confusion.

00:16:47.408 --> 00:16:48.976
We have less than three minutes!

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.878
Hey, hurry up!

00:16:52.013 --> 00:16:53.080
Sensei, sorry about this…

00:16:55.616 --> 00:16:56.450
Sensei…

00:17:09.964 --> 00:17:11.599
You're just as I expected, Kyuu-kun.

00:17:11.933 --> 00:17:14.135
I agree with your reasoning.

00:17:16.137 --> 00:17:21.375
Right after the second explosion,
I searched around myself.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:26.113
I did that because I knew I was the culprit's target.

00:17:27.348 --> 00:17:32.453
However, the bomb was nowhere to be seen.

00:17:33.187 --> 00:17:35.056
Then, where could the bomb be?

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:36.357
Kyuu!

00:17:37.692 --> 00:17:39.427
We have less than a minute before the explosion!

00:17:40.194 --> 00:17:41.896
Time's running out!

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.098
This isn't good, Kyuu!

00:17:50.238 --> 00:17:51.472
I won't give up!

00:17:52.506 --> 00:17:57.011
If a detective gives up, the
case may never be solved!

00:17:59.814 --> 00:18:02.116
You idiot! Don't just say stuff like that.

00:18:05.453 --> 00:18:07.788
If it wasn't planted on Dan-sensei…

00:18:08.522 --> 00:18:09.857
What are you doing!?

00:18:13.027 --> 00:18:13.995
Katagiri-sensei!

00:18:17.598 --> 00:18:21.202
Is there something unusual around
you, Katagiri-sensei?

00:18:21.602 --> 00:18:23.104
What? Something unusual?

00:18:24.972 --> 00:18:25.640
I got it!

00:18:31.245 --> 00:18:32.446
Her schedule book pen!

00:18:32.947 --> 00:18:34.315
In the morning there was only one.

00:18:35.516 --> 00:18:37.084
But there are two now!

00:18:39.053 --> 00:18:41.155
Oh, no! There's no time left!

00:18:45.326 --> 00:18:46.661
Up you go!

00:18:47.028 --> 00:18:48.062
W-Why!?

00:18:48.529 --> 00:18:50.531
Why did you throw it straight up?

00:18:52.867 --> 00:18:53.834
O-oh, no!

00:19:04.145 --> 00:19:05.112
W-why?

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.248
It didn't explode.

00:19:07.848 --> 00:19:10.151
That pen wasn't the bomb?

00:19:11.052 --> 00:19:13.120
So that means… We were wrong?

00:19:16.557 --> 00:19:20.094
Hand me that schedule book, Katagiri-kun.

00:19:20.761 --> 00:19:21.529
Okay.

00:19:27.601 --> 00:19:31.072
The pen that you guys were talking
about is this one, right?

00:19:31.372 --> 00:19:32.573
T-that's it.

00:19:33.474 --> 00:19:37.378
Don't worry. The time bomb
has already been removed.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.450
When I discovered that the bomb
wasn't planted on me…

00:19:42.883 --> 00:19:46.320
…I thought he might have targeted Katagiri-kun,
who is always by my side.

00:19:46.854 --> 00:19:47.822
Sensei…

00:19:48.489 --> 00:19:49.290
Thank goodness!

00:19:50.124 --> 00:19:52.259
So it won't explode.

00:19:52.493 --> 00:19:57.231
Awesome! He had already solved the trick!

00:19:57.431 --> 00:20:00.368
They're's no mistaking the legendary detective!

00:20:01.068 --> 00:20:03.237
So this is an example of Dan-sensei's
reasoning skills.

00:20:03.771 --> 00:20:07.008
No. Your reasoning was something else, too.

00:20:08.042 --> 00:20:09.377
Students of Class Q.

00:20:26.927 --> 00:20:30.664
I was the one who removed the bomb.

00:20:48.649 --> 00:20:52.253
Follow me. I'll show you guys to Class Q.

00:21:03.197 --> 00:21:06.033
This is a bit different from the main campus, isn't it?

00:21:06.367 --> 00:21:09.503
Different in that it's more run down perhaps.

00:21:22.516 --> 00:21:26.387
Look over there. That's the
building for your Class Q.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:33.828
T-that is?

00:21:34.495 --> 00:21:35.830
It looks like a haunted house.

00:21:36.363 --> 00:21:40.634
Awesome! The school building
looks like a mystery in itself!

00:21:41.535 --> 00:21:42.770
Let's hurry inside!

00:21:44.338 --> 00:21:46.640
Is it just that Kyuu's a real optimist?

00:21:46.807 --> 00:21:48.909
Or is it that he's got a few screws loose?

00:21:49.143 --> 00:21:50.277
That's the mystery, isn't it?

00:21:51.245 --> 00:21:54.748
It's already been 40 years since then…

00:21:55.282 --> 00:21:57.451
When I was a police detective…

00:21:57.451 --> 00:22:01.922
…I had my doubts about the rapidly changing
institutionalized investigatory practices.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:05.926
That doubt compelled me to retire
from the police department.

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:09.196
As a result, I made my first step towards
becoming a private investigator.

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:12.166
This was the place where I made that first step.

00:22:13.567 --> 00:22:17.638
So this is where the legendary detective
Dan Morihiko started out?

00:22:18.439 --> 00:22:19.974
It hasn't changed a bit…

00:22:20.474 --> 00:22:22.843
No matter how much the times change…

00:22:22.877 --> 00:22:26.347
…the scenic view from here hasn't changed
from the way it was in the past.

00:22:28.149 --> 00:22:35.055
I would like to perform my last job as a detective by
going back to that starting point of 40 years ago.

00:22:35.823 --> 00:22:40.361
With the passion I had when facing
crimes on my own back then…

00:22:40.794 --> 00:22:44.999
…I intend to give everything I've learned
as a detective to you new students.

00:22:55.676 --> 00:23:04.385
In conclusion, the DDS notebook that was handed
out today is the proof that you are students of DDS.

00:23:05.419 --> 00:23:10.991
Once again, to all of you newly-enrolled students,
congratulations on your acceptance!

00:23:36.104 --> 00:23:48.434
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:49.744 --> 00:24:01.594
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:01.594 --> 00:24:08.684
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:08.684 --> 00:24:14.314
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:14.514 --> 00:24:20.524
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:20.654 --> 00:24:26.074
I will see you off.

00:24:26.324 --> 00:24:35.914
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.076 --> 00:24:39.479
A flower pot shatters, the soil scatters out…

00:24:39.646 --> 00:24:42.182
…and the superficial happiness
of a family is revealed.

00:24:42.615 --> 00:24:45.185
Kazuma decodes a message from the dead.

00:24:45.618 --> 00:24:49.322
What did the victim want to tell to the
people left behind in this world?

00:24:49.923 --> 00:24:52.625
Can a computer decode this encrypted message?

00:24:53.660 --> 00:24:54.727
There's only one answer!

00:24:58.398 --> 00:25:00.266
Are you going back home, Ryuu?

00:25:01.034 --> 00:25:04.103
I don't have a place that I can
call home like you do, Kate.

00:25:04.637 --> 00:25:07.106
Then, call Kate's home your home!

00:25:07.874 --> 00:25:10.276
Ryuu!!
